{"name":"Ghee Yellow","hex":"#d8bc23","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ghee","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of clarified butter used in South Asian cooking.","Vegetable oil for cooking."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ghee"},{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ghee","blocks":[{"text":"Ghee is a type of clarified butter, originating in the Indian Subcontinent. It is a widely used butter for cooking especially in Indian cuisines and in Hindu religious rituals. Typically made from cow butter or buffalo butter, ghee is favoured for its nutty flavour and high smoke point allowing it to be heated at high temperatures without burning."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghee","wikidata":"Q323225"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow","wikidata":"Q943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Cream_to_get_clarified_butter_home_made.Ghee.jpg/500px-Cream_to_get_clarified_butter_home_made.Ghee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Cream_to_get_clarified_butter_home_made.Ghee.jpg/1280px-Cream_to_get_clarified_butter_home_made.Ghee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Cream_to_get_clarified_butter_home_made.Ghee.jpg/500px-Cream_to_get_clarified_butter_home_made.Ghee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In the cream butter method, cream is separated from milk and churned to produce butter. The butter then undergoes heat clarification.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACream_to_get_clarified_butter_home_made.Ghee.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Food_Fair_%282025%29_11.jpg/500px-Food_Fair_%282025%29_11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Food_Fair_%282025%29_11.jpg/1280px-Food_Fair_%282025%29_11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Food_Fair_%282025%29_11.jpg/500px-Food_Fair_%282025%29_11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ghee packaged in jars","link